ção"],["shaping discourse","moldar o discurso"]]}]},{"tag":"Leitura","title":"Reading · A short report","blocks":[{"type":"text","title":"Report: Reading Closely","paras":["Close readers **do not assume** that a text means what it seems; they **presume** nothing without evidence. **The more** they read, **the less** they **take for granted**. A novel may **give voice to** a grievance or **give rise to** a debate; **given that** readers differ, its meaning is never **fixed**.","**For all its** apparent simplicity, a story may **preclude** a single reading. **That said**, not every reading is **equally good**. **What matters is not** the number of interpretations **but** their **support**. **Where a reading falters** is where the text **stops answering**."],"kicker":"REPORT","by":"Literary Society","gloss":[["close reading","leitura atenta"],["fixed","fixo"],["support","fundamentação"],["apparent","aparente"]]}]},{"tag":"Compreensão","title":"Did you understand?","blocks":[{"type":"tfng","title":"","items":[{"q":"Close readers assume the text means what it seems.","ans":"F","why":"do not assume."},{"q":"Every reading is equally good, says the report.","ans":"F","why":"not every reading is equally good."},{"q":"What matters is the support of an interpretation.","ans":"T","why":"their support."}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Vocabulary in context","items":[{"q":"“give rise to” = ?","opts":["originar","dar altura","subir"],"ans":0,"why":"give rise to."},{"q":"“preclude” = ?","opts":["impedir de antemão","prever","precisar"],"ans":0,"why":"preclude."}]}]},{"tag":"Gramática","title":"Grammar recap","blocks":[{"type":"table","head":["Verifique","Exemplo"],"rows":[["**presume × assume**","**presume** (com evidência) × **assume** (ponto de partida)"],["**give**","**give rise to / give voice to / given that**"],["**Contraste e concessão**","**For all its… That said, What matters is not… but…**"],["**Comparativo duplo**","**The more… the less…**"],["**Análise literária**","técnica →